   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy 2 Outcome 1 
Implementation Period: Apr 01, 2021 - Sep 30, 2021</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy 2: Reform Area 2: Access to finance for underserved market segments improved
Outcome 1: Objective: Mitigate liquidity constraints of CMSMEs affected by COVID-19, and ensure economic recovery:

Policy: 
(i) The government implemented a new refinance scheme entitled &amp;quot;Refinance Scheme, 2020, for low-income professionals, farmers, and marginal/micro businessmen&amp;quot;, and
directed Bangladesh Bank to allocate Tk30 billion, and earmarked 25% for women borrowers; and 
(ii) To enhance access to credit for women CMSME entrepreneurs and restoring the sustainable economic recovery through term loans / investment, Bangladesh Bank amended the Small Enterprise Refinance Scheme by allowing up to TK15 billion (instead of Tk8.5 billion) at a concessional interest rate of 7% instead of 9%. 
 
Action 1: Access to finance
Target date: 
2021-09-30</narrative>
    </description>
